.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fIfmt\fR
Output format. One of: text, json. The default is text.
.TP
\fB\-\-session\fR \fIid\fR
Session id to operate on (prefix\-matched); equivalent to the positional
argument.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose output.
.TP
\fB\-\-hours\fR \fIn\fR
Time window in hours used only to resolve a session prefix; 0 applies no
filter. The default is 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fIname\fR
Restrict to matching users: a comma\-separated list of user ids or email
