\fB\-\-session\fR \fIid\fR
Restrict to a single session by id (prefix\-matched).
.TP
\fB\-\-hours\fR \fIn\fR
Time window in hours; 0 searches all history (the default). The default is 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fR
Search all history (explicit alias for the default).
.TP
\fB\-\-context\fR \fIn\fR
Lines of context to show around each match. The default is 2.
.TP
\fB\-\-role\fR \fIrole\fR
Restrict matches to one message role. One of: user, assistant, all. The
default is all.
.TP
\fB\-\-source\fR \fIsrc\fR
Restrict matches by content source kind. One of: content, tool\-input,
tool\-result, all. The default is content.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-results\fR \fIn\fR
Cap how many match rows are rendered; 0 means no cap. The default is 50.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-line\-length\fR \fIn\fR
Cap rendered snippet length per row; 0 means no cap. The default is 200.
.TP
\fB\-\-list\fR
Print one matching session per line instead of per\-match rows.
.TP
\fB\-\-count\fR
Print one matching session per line with its hit count.
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fIfmt\fR
Output format for the active mode. One of: text, json. The default is text.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-output json.
.TP
\fB\-\-regex\fR
Treat the query as a PCRE2 regular expression.
.TP
\fB\-\-case\-sensitive\fR
Case\-sensitive matching (default: case\-insensitive).
.TP
\fB\-\-user\fR \fIname\fR
Restrict to matching users: a comma\-separated list of user ids or email
addresses, where an id matches exactly and an email address matches
case\-insensitively. Only a session read from a Compliance API export carries
either, so on a machine without an export, or without the Enterprise license
that reading one needs, every \-\-user value matches nothing.
